{{!--
  A Tier 1 benefit the viewing member does not hold, rendered where the control
  it unlocks would otherwise sit. The member learns the feature exists and what
  unlocks it, and gets the one control they can act on, in place of a control
  that would refuse them. The static card variant, because the card itself is
  not clickable and should not lift under the pointer as if it were; the inline
  variant, because one statement and one action read across rather than stacking
  into a band taller than what they say.

  Caller passes:
    notice — { lead, explanation, upgradeLabel, upgradeHref } shaped by the service
--}}
<div class="card card-static card-inline">
  <p>{{notice.lead}} {{notice.explanation}}</p>
  <a href="{{notice.upgradeHref}}" class="btn btn-primary">{{notice.upgradeLabel}}</a>
</div>
